# Neo Learn Formant parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.11). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnFormant
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnFormant
class NeoLearnFormantMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching vowel synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A glottal pulse (round to buzzing, with a sub and drive) and breath noise through four formant band-pass filters that move across the vowels A, E, I, O and U, with the tract size, the formants' Q and a talking envelope that sweeps the vowel on every key, an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for choirs, talking basses, robot voices and whispers, or to learn how formants make vowels.

group Core
VowelMorph       "Vowel (A-E-I-O-U)" 0 1000 0 pct
    id vowel_morph
    how Continuously interpolates the center frequencies of the four formant bandpass filters across A -> E -> I -> O -> U.
    sound Makes the synth articulate distinct human vowel sounds as you turn the knob.
TractScale       "Tract Size" 0 1000 500 bip
    id vocal_tract_scale
    how Shifts all four formant frequencies down or up in unison without changing the played musical pitch.
    sound Changes the perceived singer from a giant deep bass (-100%) to a baritone (0%) to a high soprano/child (+100%).
FormantQ         "Formant Q" 0 1000 350 pct
    id formant_resonance
    how Controls the bandwidth (sharpness) of the four resonant vocal tract filter peaks.
    sound Lower values sound like warm, natural choir pads; high values sound intensely nasal and robotic, like a talking machine.
GlottalEdge      "Glottal / Bass" 0 1000 400 pct
    id glottal_edge
    how Shapes the excitation pulse sharpness and adds sub-glottal harmonic distortion before the formant bank.
    sound At low values the voice is soft and choral; at high values it becomes an aggressive "talking" synth bass.
BreathAir        "Breath Noise" 0 1000 100 pct
    id breath_air
    how Mixes aspirated noise into the vocal tract filters alongside the pitched pulse.
    sound Adds whispery air, human breathiness, and wind-like choir textures.
TalkingEnv       "Talking Env" 0 1000 500 bip
    id vowel_env_mod
    how Uses the note envelope to automatically sweep Vowel on every key press.
    sound Makes each note articulate syllables like "Wah", "Yah", or "Yoi" automatically.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 250 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 594 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 700 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 515 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 581 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnFormantMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
